Attribution of algorithm sources
================================

Every cryptographic primitive, checksum, and protocol framing in this
repository is an INDEPENDENT clean-room implementation written from public
specifications (IETF RFCs, NIST FIPS publications, and academic papers). No
third-party source code was copied or adapted. Under the idea/expression
dichotomy (Directive 2009/24/EC art. 1.2; Spain, art. 96.4 TRLPI; U.S.,
17 U.S.C. 102(b); CJEU C-406/10 SAS v. WPL), an algorithm is not protected by
copyright (only a specific source expression is), so these re-derived
implementations carry only this project's own license.

The specification each file implements is cited in that file's header. Where
a NIST FIPS test vector is reused it is public domain (17 U.S.C. 105). No
IETF RFC "Code Component" (ABNF grammar, pseudocode block, or test vector,
Revised BSD via the IETF Trust Legal Provisions) is reproduced verbatim; all
such algorithms are re-implemented from the prose.

See docs/licensing-and-attribution.md for the full policy.
